THINK need slewing_ring: Lets a whole upper structure rotate on a base. Big turntables have teeth so a gear can drive the rotation. Rules: Base fixed to the chassis on at least two points; top carries everything above. The pinion's shaft must be fixed to the turning half so it walks round the ring.
THINK why This big turntable has two halves that turn against each other, with 24 teeth inside and 56 outside for a gear to drive later.
THINK role turntable-O in the swing ring (turntable): The joint between lower and upper machine: fixed half pinned to the chassis, turning half carries the whole upper body.
