THINK need worm_drive: Big slow-down in one step, and self-locking: the gear can't turn the worm back, so the output holds its position (e.g. a boom stays up). Rules: Worm shaft at 90 degrees to the wheel's shaft, worm touching the wheel's teeth. The worm pushes along its own shaft: both sides need a stop or the worm slides out of mesh.
THINK why A worm only turns the gear, never the other way, so the upper body stays where you leave it.
THINK role axle8s-1 in the front worm drive (knob-2): Worm shaft running to the back: knob-2 at one end, worm-1 in the middle.
THINK role conn3-2 in the front worm drive (knob-2): Holds the worm shaft in line.
THINK role worm-1 in the front worm drive (knob-2): The self-locking slow-down: one knob turn = one tooth of crown-1.
THINK role bush-26 in the front worm drive (knob-2): Keeps the worm in place over crown-1.
